# Malamet Brawler: "target attacking creature gains trample until end of turn." Attacking with Grizzly Bears too, Bot1 targets the Bears (the
# Brawler itself and the Bears are both legal; Bot1's Elvish Mystic, not attacking, and Bot2's Elvish Mystic, not attacking for Bot2, are
# refused). Bot2 blocks each attacker with a 1/1 Elvish Mystic: the Bears (2/2, trample) assign 1 to theirs and 1 to Bot2, who goes to 19,
# but the Brawler has no trample and its excess damage is not assigned to the player, so Bot2 stays at 19, not 18.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Malamet Brawler
Grizzly Bears
Elvish Mystic
Island
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Fyndhorn Elves
Elvish Mystic
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Malamet Brawler.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Fyndhorn Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
[T5 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Malamet Brawler > Bot2; Grizzly Bears > Bot2)
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears)
Bot2.Block(Elvish Mystic > Malamet Brawler; Fyndhorn Elves > Grizzly Bears)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot2.Graveyard = Fyndhorn Elves; Elvish Mystic
